cammap is two things under two licences: the code that draws the map,
and the record of cameras it draws. They are separated here because
the licences that suit software and the licences that suit a database
are not the same, and a single one would fit one of them badly.

  THE CODE   MIT, below. Everything in this repository that is not
             the record: the HTML pages, frontend/, tools/, backend/
             schema.sql, the stylesheet. (lib/ and fonts/ are vendored
             third-party work under their own licences, unchanged, and
             are not ours to license.)

  THE DATA   The Open Database License 1.0, further below. The record
             of cameras: data/points.js, backend/seed.sql, and any
             download of the same record the site offers (a CSV or
             GeoJSON of the cameras is the same data in another form).

The copyright holder is named as "cammap contributors" because the
site puts no names on itself, on principle, and its licence should not
be the one place it does.


